  "upload": {
    "title": "The \"Bladeless\" Fan Has a Secret 🌀 #shorts",
    "description": "Dyson's Air Multiplier has no visible blades: air is pushed up into a hollow ring and forced out of a thin slit, and the ring's airfoil shape draws surrounding room air along with it. Dyson says this multiplies the airflow up to 15 times, giving a smoother breeze with no exposed spinning blades. The twist: it isn't bladeless at all. A brushless motor in the base spins an impeller (blades) that sucks the air in; they're just hidden where you can't see them.",
